   To follow up on Dave's posting I'd like to add three other ways to
get holy water.

1. Potions of holy water are sometimes randomly generated by the game.
   Take a few potions and make ordinary water by #dipping them in a
   fountain, #dipping a unicorn horn into them or zapping them with
   a wand of cancellation. Once you get potions of water use these to
   test the clear potions which you'll find lying about the dungeon
   (you can also use a scroll of identify). #dip a potion of water
   into the unidentified clear potion. If it's holy water your potion
   of water will glow blue. Your potion of water is now holy water.

2. Holy water can sometimes be purchased in a shop. A potion of
   enchanted water can be identified by the price the shopkeeper
   charges (although I believe that the same price is charged for
   both holy and unholy water).

3. Assuming that you've found an altar of *some* sort, pile up
   a bunch of blessed potions which may be identified as such by the
   altar. When you're done, zap the pile with a wand of polymorph.
   Items retain their blessed/cursed state under polymorph. Once
   you generate a clear potion - you've got holy water.

